hadiths[63]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2609","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One of us asked for his slave to be freed after his death. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called this slave and sold him. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He died in the first year. \n It was said to Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him: Are you convinced of Ghulam Mudbar's allegiance? He said: This is what the scholars say."
"2610","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a man's slave-girl gives birth to the child of her master"","" she is free after the death of that master.\"""""""
"2611","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prayed: \O Allah! Bless them in their measure"","" Bless them in their Sa'a and Mad'.\"" He meant the people of Madinah."""""
"2612","Sayyiduna Bilal said: I had a bunch of dates belonging to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I found better dates for one saa and two saar's. I submitted that I have bought one saa by giving two saa. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Give them back and give us back our dates.\"""""""
"2613","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri and Sayyidna Abu Hurairah (may God be pleased with them) narrated the hadith that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Banuadi’s brother as an agent (officer or tehsildar) to Khyber, and he brought Junib (good dates) from there. He replied: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah! All were not like this, we buy one saa of this (juneeb) by giving two saa of jum (namely junk dates). The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not do this"","" but buy and sell something equal (in weight and measure) like it"","" or sell it and buy a junib (good date) with its price"","" and do the same with weighing items.\"""""""
"2614","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \If you sell gold in exchange for gold"","" it should be in cash (no loan"","" similarly) in exchange for silver"","" it should be in cash"","" and in exchange for dates"","" dates in cash"","" and in exchange for wheat"","" wheat in cash. There should not be too much or too little in between."""""
"2615","Abu Ash-Shaath Sanani said: During the reign of Sayyidna Muawiya, may Allah be pleased with him, people began to sell gold and silver vessels until they were paid (i.e., they began to buy and sell gold or silver vessels as loans from dirhams and dinars). By selling corn for dates, barley for barley, salt for salt, but equally and in cash, so the one who gave more or took more became Rabi (interest)."
"2616","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Usury is only in the form of debt.\"" Imam al-Darmi"","" may God have mercy on him"","" said: That is"","" he should pay two dirhams for (one) dirham. (So there is interest)."""""
"2617","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I used to sell camels to Baqi, I sold them for dinars, and then I used to take dirhams, and when I sold them for dirhams, I used to take dinars (in some hadiths, the derivation is aqzab, the meaning of both is the same). Hold on, I have a question for you. I sell camels to Baqi's for dinars and take dirhams, and sometimes I sell camels for dirhams and take dinars. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \There is no wrongdoing if you take it at the same day's rate (price) as long as you do not part with each other leaving the remainder (i.e. parting without accounting).\"""""""
"2618","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, his armor was pledged to a Jew for 30 sa's of barley."
"2619","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Madinah, the people of Medina used to pay the price of fruits for two and three years in advance, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When paying the price of fruits in advance"","" find out the measure"","" weigh"","" and determine the weight.\"" \n Sufyan"","" may God bless him and grant him peace"","" used to mention the imprisonment of the time \""till a certain time\"" (ie the period is fixed)"","" then Abdullah bin Kathir cast doubt on him."""""
"2620","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid off his debt and gave him more."
"2621","It was narrated from Sweid bin Qays that Mukharama Abdi and I brought cloth from Bahrain to Makkah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us on foot and bought pajamas from us or bought them from us. There was a weigher who used to weigh for wages."
"2622","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \It is wrong for a rich person to delay in paying a debt"","" and if one of you is given a debt to a rich person"","" he should accept it.\"""""""
"2623","Abdullah bin Ka'b narrated from his father Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may God be pleased with him) that he demanded a loan from Abdullah bin Abi Hadard in the Prophet's Mosque. He said: \I am here"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" He indicated"","" \""Forgive half of the debt.\"" Sayyiduna Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I forgave half of the debt. He said: \""Ibn Abi Hadard! Get up and pay half the debt.\"""""""
"2624","Sayyiduna Abul Asir (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Whoever gives respite to the needy (debtor)\"" or said: \""Whoever forgives the debt of the needy"","" Allah will grant him shade on the Day when there will be no shade except his shade.\"" \n The narrator said: Sayyidna Abu Walisar (RA) called for the testament in which the debt was written and erased it and said to his debtor"","" \""Go"","" I have forgiven\"" and told him that he too was once needy and in need."""""
"2625","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Whoever gives respite to his debtor or forgives his debt will be under the shadow of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection.\"""""""
"2626","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A person who finds his wealth in the possession of a person while he has been declared bankrupt"","" then the owner of the wealth will be more deserving of it than others.\"""""""
"2627","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The life of a believer will be suspended as long as he has a debt.\"" \n Meaning: She will not be able to enter Paradise or that she will not get rest"","" she will remain hanging."""""
"2628","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from a freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: \He whose soul is separated from his body and he is free from three things will go to Paradise: arrogance"","" theft"","" and debt.\"""""""
"2629","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah that a funeral procession was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so that he (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) prayed over it. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Pray for your companion because he has a debt.\"" Sayyiduna Abu Qutada (RA) said: That debt or the Messenger of Allah is my responsibility (i.e. I will pay it). He said: \""I will pay in full.\"" Said: I will pay in full. Then he (PBUH) offered the funeral prayer over him."""""
"2630","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"","" I am the closest to any believer on earth (i.e. I am his guardian and responsible)"","" so whoever leaves a debt or children"","" I am responsible for him"","" and whoever leaves any property"","" that property belongs to his heirs"","" who are Baha'i.\"" \n Imam al-Darmi"","" may God have mercy on him"","" said: \""Ziy'a\"" means children and \""Fal-Ud'a\"" means that I should be called so that I can pay his debt."""""
"2631","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: \Allah is with the debtor until he repays his debt"","" unless the debt is for an act which Allah dislikes.\"" The narrator said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Jafar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say to his treasurer: Go and get a loan for me because I do not like to spend a single night without Allah being with me after I heard this from the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him)."""""
"2632","Sayyidna Samura bin Jundab (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \It is obligatory on the hand to return what it takes.\"""""""
"2633","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Repay the trust of the one who trusts you"","" and do not betray the one who betrays you.\"""""""
"2634","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a bowl containing Thareed and he (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) was in the house of another wife. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tied it and began to pour thareed into it. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying. \Eat"","" your mother became jealous\"""","" then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waited until the correct bowl arrived"","" then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the bowl to the wife whose bowl was broken. \n Imam al-Darmi"","" may God have mercy on him"","" said: Our opinion is the same (i.e. if someone breaks a cup"","" he should replace it with another clean cup)."""""
"2635","On the authority of Amr and Asim, the sons of Sufyan bin Abdullah al-Thaqafi, that their father Sufyan bin Abdullah found a leather bag, and he brought it to Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and he said: Announce it for a year, and if it is recognized, then it is fine (i.e., if its owner recognizes it, give it to him), if it is not recognized, then it is for you. Next year, Sufyan met Sayyidna Umar about her and mentioned her, then Sayyidna Umar said: She is yours. This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given about the fallen thing. Sufyan said: I don't need him, so Sayyiduna Umar took him and entered Baitul-Mal."
"2636","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that on the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and said: \Allah"","" the Exalted"","" prevented the elephants from Mecca"","" but conquered it for the sake of His Messenger and the Muslims. Look! This Mecca was not lawful for anyone before me (i.e. fighting in Mecca)"","" and it will not be lawful for anyone after me. Listen! From this time onwards"","" Mecca (fighting in Mecca) is forbidden"","" do not cut thorns here"","" nor cut down trees.\"" Go"","" no fallen thing here should be picked up except by the person who announces it"","" that is"","" the one who intends to deliver the thing to its owner"","" only he can pick up the fallen thing.\"""""""
"2637","Jarood said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \To take (the lost) thing of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire.\"""""""
"2638","Jarood said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The lost thing of a Muslim is the burning of fire"","" the lost thing of a Muslim is the burning of fire"","" the lost thing of a Muslim is the burning of fire"","" do not go near it.\"" Jarod said: A Companion said: O Messenger of Allah! What if we find a fallen object? He said: \""Announce it"","" don't hide it"","" don't make it disappear. If its owner comes"","" hand it over to him"","" otherwise"","" it is Allah's wealth"","" He gives it to whom He wills.\"" (That is"","" if no one comes to take it"","" you can take it"","" Allah has given it to you)."""""
"2639","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Umamah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever takes the right of a Muslim by (false) oath"","" Allah has made Hellfire obligatory for him and Paradise forbidden for him.\"" He said: \""Even if there is only a branch of the pilu tree.\"""""""
"2640","Sayyidna Abu Umamah al-Harithi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated a similar hadith from this chain of narrators. The translation is above."
"2641","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \On the Day of Resurrection"","" Allah will not speak to three people"","" nor will He look at them"","" nor will He purify them"","" and for them will be a painful punishment.\"" I said: O Messenger of Allah! Who are such poor people? He said: \""The one who hangs his azar below his ankles"","" the one who shows kindness"","" and the one who sells his property under false oath.\"""""""
"2642","Sayyidna Saeed bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: \Whoever takes a piece of land from someone unjustly"","" a collar of seven lands will be worn on him (on the Day of Resurrection).\"""""""
"2643","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) reported that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever settles an empty"","" uninhabited land"","" there is a reward in it"","" and whoever eats from its cultivation"","" it is a charity for him.\"" Imam Darmi"","" may God have mercy on him"","" said: Aafia means birds etc."""""
"2644","Sayyidna Abayd bin Jamal (RA) narrated that he asked the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) for a salt mine in the estate, which was called the valley or mine of Salt Marab or Sad Ma'rab. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him that valley of salt, then Sayyidna Iqra bin Habs Tamimi (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Prophet of Allah! I passed through it during the period of Jahiliyyah. It is a land in which there is no water, and whoever goes there brings salt, it does not end like stagnant deep water. Therefore, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked Sayyiduna Abayd, may God be pleased with him, to cancel this estate of salt. It is charity and like the remaining water that whoever comes there takes it.” That is, every person should benefit from it and it will never end. Sayyiduna Abayd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him land and palm trees in Jouf or Jouf Murad in exchange for this cancellation. Narrator of Hadith Faraj bin Saeed said: That salt mine remains the same till today, whoever goes there takes something from it."
"2645","Alqamah bin Wail narrated from his father Sayyiduna Wail (RA), who said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) gave him a piece of land in Jagir and sent Sayyiduna Muawiya (RA) with me to hand over that land to him. \n Yahya said: Muhammad bin Bashar narrated this hadith to us from Ghandar."
"2646","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) says: Sayyidna Umm Mubashir (may God be pleased with him), the wife of Sayyidna Zayd bin Haritha (may God be pleased with him), said to me: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me in my garden and said: \O Umm Mubashir! Who planted these (date) trees? A Muslim or an infidel?\"" I said: Muslim. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""If a Muslim plants a tree and then a person"","" animal"","" or bird eats from it"","" it is a charity for him (that is"","" a Muslim who plants a tree is rewarded for giving charity).\"""""""
"2647","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abayd bin Jamal, may Allah be pleased with him, he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for permission to demarcate Pilu, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \It cannot be stopped (delimitation) in Pilu.\"" He said: Are these yellow ones inside my field? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""There is no cover in the yellow.\"" \n Faraj (Ibn Saeed) Ibn Abayd said: Hizari refers to the land in which cultivation has been surrounded (i.e. it has been stopped by making a fence or ditch etc.)."""""
"2648","Sayyidna Iyas bin Abd Muzni (RA) said that he was one of the companions of the Prophet (PBUH). Do not sell water because I heard from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade the sale of water. \n Amr bin Dinar said: I don't know which water he forbade to sell. He said: They say that it is not known whether he forbade running water or drinking water."
"2649","Bahisa narrated from his father: He told the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he attended the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked his permission, then he put his mouth inside and began to embrace (kiss), then he said: What is not permissible to prevent? He said: \With salt and water.\"" Then asked: What is the thing from which it is not permissible to prevent? He said: \""The more good you do"","" the better.\"" Then asked: What is not permissible to prevent? He said: \""It is better to do as much good as you can\"" and he satisfied himself only with salt and water. Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? He nodded his head."""""
"2650","It was narrated from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, made an agreement with the people of Khyber to cultivate and divide half of the dates."
"2651","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the communication, we used to give one-third or half of the land for cultivation for two or three years. (i.e. do not drive for hire).”"
"2652","Abdullah bin Sa'ib said: I asked Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) about mujarat, and he said: Sayyidna Thabit bin Dahhak Ansari (RA) told me that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade mujarat (i.e. giving land for sowing). The narrator asked Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him: Do you also say the same thing? He said: No, I am convinced of the first opinion."
"2653","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the sale of vacant land for two or three years."
"2654","Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (RA) said: We used to rent land during the time of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) for the amount of produce that was on the banks of the canals and on which water would flow automatically, but the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) stopped us from doing so and allowed us to rent the land in exchange for gold or silver (i.e. in exchange for dirhams and dinars)."
"2655","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Masood bin Nayyar (RA) that Sayyidna Sahl Bin Abi Hatmah (RA) came to our meeting and narrated the hadith that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \When you estimate (fruits on trees)"","" take (two-thirds) and leave one-third"","" if not one-third"","" leave one-fourth.\"""""""
"2656","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earning (of adultery) of slave girls."
"2657","Sayyidna Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \The earnings of a horn-planter are bad (i.e. taking the wages of a horn-planter is bad)"","" and the earnings of a prostitute are bad"","" and taking the price of a dog is bad.\"""""""
"2658","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that Abu Taybah (Nafi'a or Maysara) put a horn on the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and he ordered him to pay him two sa's of grain."
"2659","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade taking the price of the water (semen) of a male (animal)."
"2660","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade taking wages for the water of a male and also forbade taking the wages of an adulterous woman."
"2661","Sayyiduna Saeed bin Harith, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had the privilege of being in the company of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Whoever among you sells a house or land"","" it is possible that his money will not be blessed unless he invests the price in another house.\"""""""
"2662","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever digs a well"","" it is not permissible for anyone else to dig a well up to forty cubits around to feed and feed his animals (ie: forty cubits around the well should be left for the one who digs the well).\"""""""
"2663","On the authority of Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about intercession: \When the path of two neighbors is the same"","" he (the neighbor) will be waited for through intercession"","" even if he is absent.\"""""""
"2664","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) decided to intercede in every joint matter that is not divided. Whether it is land or a garden, it is not good for one partner to sell it unless the other partner has given permission. This partner has the right to take it if he wants and if he wants to not take it. \n Imam Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) was asked: Do you also say the same? He said: Yes."
"2665","It was narrated from Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) that Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) asked Sayyidna Umar (RA) for permission to enter, but he did not get permission, so he returned. Sayyiduna Umar asked: Why did you go back? Narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \A person seeking permission should ask for permission to enter three times. If permission is granted"","" he should enter"","" otherwise he should return.\"" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You must bring a witness on this matter"","" otherwise I will treat you very badly. Sayyidna Abu Saeed (RA) said: Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) came to us and I was also present in the mosque with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). Sayyidna Abu Musa was very nervous because of Sayyidna Umar's warning to him. He stood near us and said: I swear to you people"","" if any man has heard this from the Messenger of Allah"","" may God bless him and grant him peace"","" then bear witness to it with me. Sayyidna Abu Saeed (RA) said: I raised my head and said: Tell Sayyidna Umar (RA) that I also heard this with you and the other Companions also supported him"","" so Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) was happy to hear this"""""
"2666","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and when I knocked on his door, he (PBUH) said: \Who is this?\"" I said: I am"","" he said: \""I"",""\"" that is"","" he disliked it."""""
"2667","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade a man to come to his house at night to catch the treachery or theft of his family members, or to find their fault. \n Sufyan said: I don't know whether \Yakhonham\"" and \""Yiltams ghadatham\"" were said by Muhareb on his own behalf or are they the words of hadith?"""""
"2668","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was coming to Madinah, people were standing in the way of him (may God bless him and grant him peace), and when he came, people came out. I was among them and when I saw the blessed face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, I said (in my heart) that it cannot be the face of a liar. At that time, the first thing I heard from the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was: \People! Spread greetings (i.e. greet each other as well)"","" feed them"","" show mercy"","" and pray when people sleep"","" and you will enter Paradise safely.\"""""""
"2669","Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Ali (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \A Muslim has six rights: When he meets a Muslim"","" he should greet him"","" when he sneezes"","" he should respond (i.e. the person who sneezes should say Alhamdulillah"","" then he should say YarahmakAllah in response)"","" if he is sick"","" he should attend to his sick person"","" when he is invited"","" he should accept it. A Muslim should like his brother and wish him well in his absence.”"""""
"2670","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Fazla bin Ubayd that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A rider should greet a pedestrian"","" and a standing person should greet a sitting person. Few people should greet many people.\"""""""
"2671","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of the Jews greets him"","" he says: \""Al-Sam-Aleek\"" (may death be upon you). In response"","" you should say: \""Alayk\"" means death upon you.\"""""""
